    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d459">

                <pb facs="0458" n="446" xml:id="pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 European War 1939/468: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-21T17:00:00+01:00">September 21,
                            1939—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 21—1:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2094. It is the opinion of the French Government that the cutting of
                    communications between Poland and Rumania by the Soviet Government is designed
                    to prevent a German attack on Rumania since the Soviet Government fears to have
                    Germany on the Black Sea and would prefer to swallow the Rumanian Black Sea
                    coast itself.</p>
                <p>The impression is strong here that the Germans may make an almost immediate
                    attack on the Netherlands. The Netherlands Minister has just been in contact
                    with his Government on this subject and assures me that his Government has no
                    fear whatsoever of immediate German attack.</p>
                <p>The conversations between the French, British and Turks are progressing
                    surprisingly satisfactorily from the French and British point of view.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
